  "limits": [
    "Original overall run remains failed; six native cases passed, React JavaScript development failed at native close, React JavaScript AOT remains not-run. Native raw-event/lifecycle review belongs to the separate native_services audit.",
    "Bun executable bytes, bootstrap/staging directories, installed node_modules and cache payloads are omitted. Compiler identity matches the pinned digest and source-bound receipts; installed inventories, exact pinned markers and contained links are original controller observations, not a post-cleanup byte reinspection.",
    "Four AOT executable bytes, launcher.ts and inner compile-aot stdout/stderr were not retained by original d09. Their actual compile/inspection/fingerprint receipts are present, but this audit cannot independently reinspect omitted executable sections or recover missing compiler logs. Later retention fixes do not replace these original omissions.",
    "All four AOT development modules/maps are retained. Their 118 mapped inputs are bound to consumer/package records; 116 embedded sources match raw input bytes. The two Solid entry sources contain the existing universal transform and are independently bound through retained original main files; original-TSX line/column fidelity is not claimed.",
    "Expected consumer inputs are checked before native attempts and after successful cases. The failed React JavaScript development command exits before its post-case expected_inputs call; no post-failure consumer-byte revalidation is inferred. Repository/package/compiler/host invariance is checked in the retained controller finalization path.",
    "Per-native wrapper reports do not independently capture repository source or native_host.path; provenance is supplied by verified outer source/package records, owner artifact fingerprints and monitored expected host identity.",
    "Observed process ownership and joined cleanup are bounded to the recorded controller contract; they are not a general heap, long-soak, hardware-GPU, display-presentation or cross-platform claim."
  ],
